WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.400
-Come on,
you gotta feel the love.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.934
We love you. We love you.
-Ah, thank you.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.100
-Katie Holmes!

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.000
-I feel the love when I come.
-You feel good, please.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.300
-It's so nice to see you.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.200
-I want to see you -- I want you
on the show every night,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.968
so, please, just stay here for
the rest of the week.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.167
-Done.
-Alright, good.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.901
I want to talk about
your play "The Wanderers,

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.634
but, first, I wanted to mention
"The Ice Storm,"

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.601
which I believe was
your film debut.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.100
It was 25 years ago.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.767
-I know.
-Can you believe that?

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.334
What do you remember about that?

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:28.067
-Well, I was 17, and I remember
we came to New York,

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.267
my mom and I.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.601
And we shot it,
and I thought, "Oh, I mean,

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:32.634
this is what I want to do.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:33.934
Great."
-You knew it.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:38.400
-And then I went home
and I was putting myself on tape

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.567
for different auditions and I
wasn't really getting anything.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:44.868
And I thought,
"Oh, well, that might be it."

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.167
You know,
that might be all there is.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.501
-"My dream."

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:48.701
-But it was okay, 'cause I was
like, "You know what?

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:49.767
That's okay.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.267
Like, that was
an amazing experience,

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.534
and I can, like, tell my
grandkids and I'll be fine."

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.067
-Oh, my gosh.
-No, seriously.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.501
-Really?
-I was like, "That's cool."

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.100
-You were happy with that?
And you go, "Yeah, that was --"

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.234
-Well, I mean,
I wanted more jobs,

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.400
but I was like,
"Don't be, you know --

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.701
I don't know -- greedy."

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:06.734
-Yeah. You didn't think --
You were like,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:07.834
"Oh, maybe it's not
going to happen."

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.167
Now you're Katie Holmes.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.400
I mean, did you go --
Do you remember the audition?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.767
-For "The Ice Storm"?
-Yeah.

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.200
-Yeah, I mean, it was --

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.634
My mom and I went out
for pilot season.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.467
We landed on a Sunday.
-I love your mom, by the way.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.567
And your sisters, by the way.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.334
-Thank you.
-But I love your mom.

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:22.567
I always give your mom
a shout-out

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.334
every time I see you
because she is the nicest.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.100
She sent me
a nice care package once,

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.434
and I'll never forget it.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:30.133
-She loves you.
-She's the greatest.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.934
I thought that was so cool
that she did that.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.167
But your mom's very supportive.
-Very supportive.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.100
And it was my second day in L.A.
and my first audition.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.534
I know. I got lucky.
-Wow!

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:43.834
Were you intimidated at all
by L.A.?

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.701
-Yeah. I remember
we got lost a lot,

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.934
because it was like,
you know, no Google Maps.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.467
It was the Thomas Guide.
-Thomas Guide!

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:50.767
-And we were lost
every single day.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.367
-I can't believe
the Thomas Guide.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.901
-Yes.
-That is the most confusing map

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.934
I've ever read
in my entire life.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.367
And you get to L.A.,
and everyone goes,

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.701
"You've got to get a
Thomas Guide."

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.133
And then it's all, like, weird.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.801
It's like,
"Okay, where are we now?"

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:04.501
I go, "Alright,
we're at A-4 or G-6."

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:05.868
I'm, like, doing the math
in my head.

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.300
I'm like, "I'm so lost."

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.100
-To this day,
when I drive in L.A.,

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.868
I know how to get around
because of all the times

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:11.968
we got lost when I was a kid.

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.934
-That's so funny.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.434
-So, you get lost
and then you go to the audition.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.567
You're already frazzled.
-Yes, exactly.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:18.968
-You're like,
"I'm sorry if I'm terrible,

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:20.267
but I don't know where I am."

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.601
-I know. One time, I went to
an audition by myself.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.968
I was older then.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.667
And I was 45 minutes late,
'cause I had gotten lost --

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:30.167
with my Thomas Guide --
and the lady yelled at me.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:33.334
And I was like,
"I really -- I tried.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:34.601
You have no idea."
-Yeah.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.033
"I really want this part,
yeah, please."

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.868
-Yeah, exactly.
-Like, "That's why I'm here."

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.501
Yeah, you do get lost.
-You get lost.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:43.267
-But I heard you stumbled into
the Golden Globes or something.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.501
-Yes, that was the other thing.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.868
Our first day in L.A.,
we were driving.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.167
It was raining.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.968
And we saw a sign that said,
"Golden Globes this way."

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:54.000
We were like, "Golden Globes?"
So we turned.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.167
And we sat in the -- Or --

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.534
Yeah, we sat in,
like, the stadium seats.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:02:59.634
-It actually was happening
as you were there?

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.133
-It was.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.234
And so we watched people getting
in and out of cars and waving.

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.834
And we were -- I mean,
it was, like, Patrick Swayze.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:08.767
-Yeah. That's so fun.
-And it was amazing.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.133
-And did you ever think,
"Oh, I'm going to be

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.534
walking this red carpet
one day"?

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:14.501
-No. But I don't --
I just didn't think about it.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:18.100
I was like, "Wow!
How did this happen?"

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.167
-Yeah, it's magic.
It's kind of fun.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.734
-Yeah, it was pretty fun.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.467
-I want to talk about your play,
but, also, I want to

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.400
talk about your movie
that you co-wrote and directed.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.701
This is your third or --
-My third film that I directed.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.000
-You got the director bug.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.868
-Yeah, I'm gonna be calling you.
-I love it.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.901
No, yeah, right.
Have you seen my acting?

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.200
-Yes, I have.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.667
-Whew! You don't want that.
-I love working with you.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.100
-No!
-We had our minute on "SNL."

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.334
-Yeah, we did.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.534
Of course, that's --
I gave you your big break.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.567
Yeah, of course.
-You did.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.167
-It's called "Rare Objects."
-It's called "Rare Objects."

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.734
It's about female friendship
and healing.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:51.334
We shot it here
in New York City.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.434
Alan Cumming is in it, as well.
-Oh, I love him.

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.934
-Yeah. And it's a --
And Julia Mayorga,

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:58.534
who's an up-and-coming actress
who's wonderful.

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:00.868
And it's, like,
a love letter to New York.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:03.067
-That comes out in April.
-April 14th.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.601
-But I love that you -- I think
you'd be a great director.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.367
I think you have a great eye.
-Well, thank you.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.067
-So this is, like -- So you're
going to keep doing this.

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.701
-I am. I love working --
-Do both?

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.067
-Yeah, I love
working with actors,

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:16.934
and then I love the visual
aspect of it, as well, yeah.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.601
-Let's talk about
"The Wanderers."

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:20.100
You're in rehearsals now.
-Yes.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.834
-Performances begin
in less than two weeks.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:24.701
-A week from Thursday,
to be exact.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.634
-Yeah, to be exact.
So it's getting real.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.367
-It's real now.
-It's real.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.234
You're like, "Okay, are we
really doing this, guys?

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.434
We're putting on a show."

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.334
-Yeah.
-I've seen you onstage before.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.567
You're fantastic.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:37.968
Do you love the risk of theater
or doing it live?

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.701
-Yeah, I mean, I do.

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:43.067
It's -- I'm -- Some actors,
you know, they get into it

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:46.434
and they get used to it
and they roll in and they do it.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:47.868
But I'm not that person.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.801
I have to read through
my lines every day

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:54.200
and I am terrified
until closing night.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.467
Because I just -- What if I'm --

00:04:56.467 --> 00:05:00.234
You know, one time, I went blank
and I forgot a line,

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:01.667
and it was so scary.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.834
-Really? But you have a whole
cast of people, too.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.434
-I know, and then I feel like
I can't let them down.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:10.434
-No, but, also, I feel like they
might lose one of their lines,

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.000
and then I've got to pick up
where they --

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.167
And I'm like,
"You're supposed to say,

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:15.501
'Close the door,' remember?"

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:18.200
-Exactly. "You were supposed to
pick that up! Aah!"

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.834
-"Aah! The door's open."

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.167
Yeah, I would just be
terrible at it.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.734
Like, oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:25.601
-It would be -- Yeah, so,
yeah, there's some risk of that.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.701
-But it's a great cast.
-It's a wonderful cast.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:31.667
Eddie Kaye Thomas,
who I haven't seen in 20 years.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.868
-Wow.
-And we've had a wonderful time.

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:38.968
And I actually --
When I'm working,

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:43.100
I tend to become
very superstitious.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.601
And --
-You do?

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:47.534
-I do. So, I have
these different rituals.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.601
So if, like,
I eat a certain meal

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.801
and the show goes well,
then I only eat that meal

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.701
for the run of the show,
which is --

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:57.100
It drives everyone
around me crazy.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.467
-'Cause you go, "Wait.

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.834
I can't believe I just had
half a Coke and a hot dog."

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:03.100
You're like,
"I have to have that

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.567
every day for the whole run"?

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.601
-Great, I've got to do
30 more minutes

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:08.501
on the bike for that meal?

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.100
-What's your go-to meal?

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.701
-Well, it's kind of boring.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.434
I mean, it's usually, like,
something light,

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:17.033
like a salad with chicken
or something.

00:06:17.033 --> 00:06:19.400
But, you know, I mean,
it would be nice to have, like,

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.334
a pepperoni pizza with
hot honey or something.

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:23.767
I mean, that would be great.

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:26.133
-Yeah, but you can't do that
every night and sustain the --

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:27.534
-But maybe after the show.

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.067
-Yeah, after the show,
we can do it.

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:30.701
What is the play about?
Can we talk --

00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:33.267
-The play -- it's about

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.801
two couples from
Brooklyn, Williamsburg.

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:37.100
-Yeah.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.200
-But it's two different
time periods.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.501
And they're related.

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:47.167
And the show touches upon
family, marriage, death.

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:52.200
And it's about human discontent
and self-examination.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.701
It's funny, it's high drama,

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:57.734
and it's definitely
that New York experience of,

00:06:57.734 --> 00:06:58.968
"I'm going to the theater."

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:00.133
-Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.033
-So you're gonna to come.
-Of course.

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:04.400
-Yeah, okay.
-I'm there.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.367
-I thought we'd do
a little champagne toast

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:07.534
before the play starts.

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:08.701
Come on. Absolutely.
You know we love you.

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:09.834
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:07:09.834 --> 00:07:11.801
Katie Holmes, everybody.
-Thank you.

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.133 --> 00:07:16.434
-"The Wanderers" begins
performances January 26th.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:19.300
Katie and I are playing a
new fun game when we come back.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.467
Stick around, everybody.

